GraphTask - BASIC programs in windows on the desktop
===================================================

In RISC OS 3.71, double-clicking a BASIC program gives it the whole
screen: nothing else runs until it ends and you press SPACE. The Task
window (Ctrl-F12) multitasks, but shows text only.

!GraphTask, in the Apps directory, runs BBC BASIC programs in windows
of their own on the desktop, graphics, colours, teletext and all. Each
window is a "graphics task window": it has its own screen mode and
palette, the program in it keeps running while you use other programs,
and you can run several at once. It is after David Ruck's !GraphTask
(DEEJ Technology, 1990-2021), which did the same on real machines.

